# Mission plan

## Objectives

1. Intake a multi-part document (template **or** given structure) under a folder
   registered in **`.sedea/documentation-management.yaml`**.
2. Produce an approved **master plan** — overview of document sections and part
   delivery order. Master-plan **`parts[]`** sizing uses **group-only word budgets**
   (350 prose / 250 filler-heavy words per part — merge adjacent units, never
   split). Unlike **Author Simple Document**, do **not** plan and render the
   entire document in one pass.
3. Deliver each part via a **part-planner** child lane **spawned by
   master-plan** (not Squad Leader) that **spawns** the **author** child for
   that part. Plan revisions flow **planner → author** (not via Squad Leader
   rebroadcast). After authoring, the author reviews the
   part conversation for SoT alterations and collects per-change approvals into
   the SoT changes follow-up document. The structure of each part plan is
   defined during that part’s planning session. Per-change approval on the
   author (or revision-author) lane records approved rows in the **SoT changes
   follow-up document** (ops docs). The **Squad Leader** applies those approved
   rows to `<localPath>/source-of-truth/` immediately after the part-planner or
   document-reviewer child terminal — without a second approval gate. It is **not**
   `<localPath>/source-of-truth/CHANGELOG.md` (audit of completed SoT writes).
   When consulting SoT while authoring a part, do **not** treat
   **`CHANGELOG.md`** as authoritative unless the user explicitly names it and
   explains how to use it (rule **20** § *Change log*).
4. Between parts, when the user requests it, **master-plan** (not Squad Leader)
   spawns a **gap-analyzer** to detect contradictions or misinterpretations across
   authored parts; when gaps are found, the **gap-analyzer** spawns **gap-closer**
   on its lane (nested spawn). After each analyzer/closer cycle, the Squad Leader
   offers **another gap analysis run** (routed to master-plan) — multiple passes
   often surface different issues.
5. Keep Squad Leader / master-plan standing options available for the whole
   active dispatch: **Generate Content**, **Sync documents**, **Export PDF**,
   continue part delivery, request gap analysis, and finish/approve content.
   After §2 folder bind, **every** Squad Leader structured-choice modal includes
   **`sync-documents`** so GDrive edits can bisync into the local folder without
   waiting for the §5 standing gate alone (§5a).
6. Support long-running authoring (hours, days, or weeks) with repeatable sync
   and content-generation passes until all parts are authored and the user
   approves the content.
7. **PDF export (Squad Leader):** On **user request**, offer the same PDF export
   modes as Author Simple Document (`documentation-folder-sync` |
   `operations-result` | `skip`), then spawn Convert Document **`pdf-converter`**.
   Do **not** auto-export after each part. Never replace the source document.
8. Close the dispatch with an explicit Squad Leader
   **`mission_control_propose_dispatch_resolution`** when the pass is complete,
   partial, or abandoned.
9. **Document comment review (optional):** After gap analysis (or on demand from
   §5), when the user opts in on the Squad Leader lane, **master-plan** (not Squad
   Leader) spawns **document-reviewer** to sync the remote document, inventory
   review comments, approve a review plan, implement revisions via a
   **revision-author** child lane, collect SoT follow-ups, and offer return to
   **gap analysis** or standing options.
10. **Master-plan plan hygiene (binding):** While the dispatch is active,
   **master-plan** maintains the approved **master plan** artifact when
   downstream work (part-planner terminals, gap analysis/closer cycles,
   document-reviewer/revision-author cycles) materially affects part order,
   scope, or high-level notes — via child terminals and
   **`mission_control_notify_child_lanes`** when plan-change notification is
   enabled.
11. **Brainstorming intake (optional):** Before master planning, the Squad Leader
    may spawn **document-brainstorm** so the **user** can explore folder docs,
    source-of-truth, and intent in a dedicated child lane. An approved brainstorm
    report pre-seeds §4 **master-plan** intake (objectives, scope, documents to
    change) without a second leader approval gate before master-plan spawn.

