## Protocol

### 1. Infer intent from the opening command phrase

- **Type:** Branching logic
- **Intent:** Match this mission’s command phrases and prepare routing.
- **Inputs:** Opening message; **`mission.yaml`** `commands`.
- **Expected output:** Intent label (`author-multi-part`).
- **Next-step resolution:** Phrase matches → §2 (auto-advance). No match →
  USER_CHECKPOINT below.

USER_CHECKPOINT — confirm intent when the opening command phrase does not match unambiguously.

- Apply **phrase matching** from [`.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/4_mission.mdc`](.sedea/centers/sedea/rules/4_mission.mdc)
  (longer phrases first).
- Map phrases from **`mission.yaml`**:
  - **`author multi-part document`** → intent **`author-multi-part`**
- After intent is mapped, run **Dispatch display refresh** when scope is readable.

### 2. Resolve documentation folder and target file context

- **Type:** Branching logic
- **Intent:** Bind this dispatch to a registered documentation folder and the
  multi-part document path (new or existing).
- **Inputs:** [`.sedea/documentation-management.yaml`](.sedea/documentation-management.yaml);
  intent from §1; user hints (folder slug, relative file path).
- **Expected output:** `folderSlug`, `localPath`, `rclone.remote`,
  `rclone.remotePath`; `relativeFilePath` under `localPath` when known.
  When §3 used a template, `relativeFilePath` **must** be the duplicated
  working file — **never** the template path.
- **Next-step resolution:** Folder resolved → §3. Missing registry or tools →
  USER_CHECKPOINT below.

Read the folder registry completely. Do **not** invent slugs, remotes, or local
roots. Preconditions follow
[`.sedea/centers/documentation-management/rules/00_documentation-management.mdc`](../../rules/00_documentation-management.mdc)
and
[`.sedea/centers/documentation-management/rules/10_required-tools.mdc`](../../rules/10_required-tools.mdc).

USER_CHECKPOINT — pick registered folder slug · provide relative file path · start Required Tools Installation in a new dispatch · abort.

### 2.5 Brainstorming intake (optional — `brainstorm-first`)

- **Type:** Agent engagement and handover
- **execution:** `spawned`
- **Intent:** Free-form exploration of folder documents and source-of-truth until
  the **user** is ready to start multi-part authoring; produce an approved
  brainstorm report for **master-plan** intake.
- **Trigger:** User selects **`brainstorm-first`** at §3 (or opening message
  states brainstorm-first after §2 folder bind).
- **Target agent role:** Document brainstorm agent
- **Assigned skill:** [`skills/document-brainstorm/SKILL.md`](skills/document-brainstorm/SKILL.md)
- **Checkpoint child UX:** Report completion USER_CHECKPOINT lives on the child
  skill — see **`document-brainstorm/SKILL.md`** § *Report completion gate*; this
  §2.5 **#external-wait** covers leader spawn-and-wait only.
- **Inputs:** Folder binding from §2 (`folderSlug`, `localPath`, rclone fields);
  `operationsDocsDirectory`; optional `brainstormTopic`, `brainstormPrompt`,
  `openingSeeds` from user message.
- **Expected output:** Child terminal with `outputs.brainstormReportPath`,
  `outputs.userApprovedReport`, `outputs.objectives[]`,
  `outputs.documentsToChange[]`, `outputs.downstreamHandoffSummary`, or
  `outputs.abandonMission: true`.
- **Next-step resolution:**
  - `userApprovedReport: true` + `continuationStatus: terminal` → compile §4
    **master-plan** spawn inputs from report (`intakeMode: structure-given` or
    derived template hints, `relativeFilePath` when known, structure outline +
    objectives from report; `brainstormReportPath` / `brainstormReportRef`) →
    **auto-chain §4** on the same leader turn (**forbidden:** repeat §3
    USER_CHECKPOINT before master-plan spawn).
  - `abandonMission: true` → §11 dispatch resolution **`abandoned`**.
  - Otherwise → USER_CHECKPOINT gate below.

USER_CHECKPOINT — pick next step when brainstorm child reports failure or partial.

**Procedure (binding)**

1. **Spawn turn:** Emit exactly one **`mission_control_spawn_agent`** for
   **`document-brainstorm`** with §2 folder binding + optional topic/prompt
   seeds — **alone** per rule **4** spawn-turn sequencing.
2. **Next turn:** After host-visible spawn confirmation, open **#external-wait**
   structured choice before StreamFinal.
3. On terminal **`userApprovedReport: true`**, record `brainstormReportPath` /
   `brainstormReportRef` on the leader ledger and emit §4 **master-plan** spawn
   (spawn turn alone) without re-collecting §3 template/structure on the leader
   lane.
4. On **`abandonMission: true`**, propose dispatch resolution — do not spawn §4.

**Checkpoint auto-chain (binding):** Under **`trustLevel: checkpoint`**, approved
brainstorm report → §4 master-plan spawn is **happy-path auto-advance** on the
leader lane — **forbidden:** USER_CHECKPOINT to re-approve starting master-plan
when report outputs include `userApprovedReport: true`.

### 3. Intake — template or structure

- **Type:** Branching logic
- **Intent:** Collect how the multi-part document is shaped before master planning.
- **Inputs:** Folder binding from §2; optional template path; optional structure
  outline from the user.
- **Expected output:** `intakeMode` = `template` | `structure-given` |
  `brainstorm-first`; when `template`: `templatePath` (read-only source) +
  `relativeFilePath` (new working document under `localPath`); when
  `structure-given`: approved structure outline; optional existing document to
  extend (non-template path only); when `brainstorm-first`: route to §2.5 until
  brainstorm completes or abandons.
- **Next-step resolution:** **`brainstorm-first`** → §2.5. Other modes: intake
  approved with a writable working document → §4. Incomplete → re-ask.

USER_CHECKPOINT — brainstorm first · use template · supply structure outline · revise intake · abort.

**Modes (binding):**

| Mode | Outcome |
|------|---------|
| **Brainstorm first** | Squad Leader spawns **document-brainstorm** (§2.5). After approved report, auto-chain §4 **master-plan** with report-derived intake — skip template/structure collection on the leader lane until brainstorm completes or abandons. |
| **Use template** | User supplies `templatePath`. Agent **duplicates** the template into a **new** working document under `localPath` (propose a new filename; confirm or revise before write). Master plan and all later edits target **only** the new file. |
| **Structure given** | User supplies section/part structure; master plan uses that outline on a new or existing **non-template** working file. |

**Template reuse (binding — Use template):**

1. Templates stay blank / reusable — **forbidden** to offer editing the template file, or to write part content / master-plan body into `templatePath`.
2. Before collecting document content or spawning part lanes, **propose a new filename** (and optional subfolder under `localPath`) via structured choice; after confirmation, **copy** the template to that path and set `relativeFilePath` to the copy.
3. Treat `templatePath` as **read-only** for structure derivation only (section headings / outline). All authoring, Generate Content, Sync of the working doc, and PDF export use `relativeFilePath`.
4. Mirror Author Simple Document create mode **Use template** → scaffold a **standard document** from the template (non-template outcome).

**Forbidden:** editing the selected template in place; treating the template path as the multi-part working document; skipping the new-filename proposal when `intakeMode` is `template`.

### 4. Author and approve master plan (spawned master-plan lane)

- **Type:** Agent engagement and handover
- **execution:** `spawned` (leader → master-plan)
- **Intent:** After §3 intake (or §2.5 auto-chain), Squad Leader spawns
  **master-plan**; the child produces a reviewable **master plan**: document
  overview, ordered parts/sections, and high-level content notes — not full part
  prose.
- **Inputs:** Intake from §3 (`intakeMode`, `relativeFilePath`, optional
  `templatePath` / structure outline) or §2.5 terminal (`brainstormReportPath`,
  `brainstormReportRef`, `structureOutline` / objectives from report); folder
  binding (`localPath`, `folderSlug`, rclone fields); `operationsDocsDirectory`.
- **Expected output:** Child milestone with `masterPlanPath`; `parts[]` with
  stable `partId` / titles, **`estimatedWordCount`**, and **`contentClass`**
  (`prose` | `filler-heavy`); `userApprovedMasterPlan: true`;
  `continuationStatus: active` (master-plan lane stays orchestrator until parts
  complete or user abandons).
- **Next-step resolution:** Child milestone after approval → §5 standing options.
  Part delivery via master-plan spawn (§6). Rejected or aborted on child lane →
  USER_CHECKPOINT on leader (retry · abort).

**Procedure (binding)**

1. Squad Leader emits **`mission_control_spawn_agent`** for
   **`skills/master-plan/SKILL.md`** with §3 + folder binding inputs.
   Set spawn **`name`** to **`Master plan`** (or a ≤64-char document title when
   known); **`description`**: one-line scope (≤512 chars).
2. Open **#external-wait** on the leader before ending the turn (wait for
   master-plan terminal).
3. **On the master-plan lane** (see `skills/master-plan/SKILL.md`): draft artifact
   under dispatch **`plans/`**; apply group-only word-budget part sizing (350
   prose / 250 filler-heavy — merge adjacent units, never split); resolve open
   questions via structured choice; **USER_CHECKPOINT** — approve master plan ·
   revise master plan · abort.
4. On approval: register **`masterPlanPath`** via
   **`mission_control_update_relevant_documents`**; emit **milestone**
   **`mission_control_send_agent_result`** with `continuationStatus: active`
   (not terminal while parts remain). **Forbidden:** master-plan lane
   **`mission_control_refocus_parent_lane`** before terminal completion; refocus on
   the same turn as post-approval milestone delivery; refocus parent and spawn
   part-planner on the same turn (part delivery follows §6 after Squad Leader §5
   handoff on a **later** master-plan turn).
5. Squad Leader records `masterPlanPath` and `parts[]`, then routes to §5.
   Master-plan lane remains active for part-planner orchestration (§6).

**Forbidden:** leader inline master-plan authoring; one-pass full-document
authoring on this step (that is Author Simple Document); Squad Leader
USER_CHECKPOINT to re-approve a plan already approved on the master-plan lane.

